      <title>5 dead after crash at Miami Airport. And, Germany's far-right wins state election</title>
      <author>Brittney Melton</author>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/09/07/g-s1-142210/up-first-newsletter-miami-plane-crash-ukraine-affirmative-for-germany</link>
      <comments>https://text.npr.org/2026/09/07/g-s1-142210/up-first-newsletter-miami-plane-crash-ukraine-affirmative-for-germany</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.npr.org/2026/09/07/g-s1-142210/up-first-newsletter-miami-plane-crash-ukraine-affirmative-for-germany</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 11:11:51 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The National Transportation Safety Board is investigating after a cargo plane crashed at Miami International Airport yesterday&lt;/strong&gt;, killing five people and injuring five others. The Amazon Prime plane was landing at the airport around 2 p.m. ET when it &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/06/nx-s1-5959749/amazon-cargo-plane-crashes-at-miami-airport" target="_blank"&gt;overran the runway and crashed&lt;/a&gt; into vehicles on the ground. It remains unclear if the people who were hurt or killed were on the plane or on the ground at the time of the collision.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-142204" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 6000;         --source-height: 3375;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+498/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2Fe80c7fac4735810cdc09b1678277%2Fgettyimages-2293852643.jpg" class="img" alt="An Amazon cargo plane is seen after it crashed at Miami International Airport on Sunday in Miami, Florida. The Federal Aviation Administration said Prime Air Flight 7598 overran the runway while landing around 2 p.m. ET after departing from San Juan, Puerto Rico." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 An Amazon cargo plane is seen after it crashed at Miami International Airport on Sunday in Miami, Florida. The Federal Aviation Administration said Prime Air Flight 7598 overran the runway while landing around 2 p.m. ET after departing from San Juan, Puerto Rico.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Joe Raedle/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;These investigations are often extensive and time-consuming&lt;/strong&gt;, because a series of cascading factors can contribute to any crash, NPR's Arezou Rezvani tells &lt;em&gt;Up First&lt;/em&gt;. Investigators will look into possible mechanical failures, flight crew performance and weather conditions. Rezvani says that airports, particularly those with shorter runways, have been concerned about incidents like these for the last couple of decades. Many have installed Engineered Materials Arresting Systems — essentially, crushable materials at the ends of runways designed to help stop planes that overrun the runway. Miami International Airport doesn't have this system in place because its runways are pretty long, which &lt;a href="https://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5960265:x" target="_blank"&gt;makes this crash more unusual&lt;/a&gt;, Rezvani says.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trump administration envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner said their meetings with Ukraine's &lt;/strong&gt;President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv yesterday &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/06/nx-s1-5959657/us-envoys-witkoff-kushner-talks-in-kyiv-putin-moscow" target="_blank"&gt;were "substantive."&lt;/a&gt; The envoys held extensive conversations with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Moscow the day before. Witkoff and Kushner want peace talks to resume, but the visit did not yield a breakthrough.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;This is the two men's first-ever wartime visit to Ukraine&lt;/strong&gt;, and that held &lt;a href="https://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5960265:x" target="_blank"&gt;significant symbolism for Zelenskyy&lt;/a&gt;, NPR's Joanna Kakissis says. White House-sponsored peace talks between Ukraine and Russia stalled after the U.S. and Israel attacked Iran in February. Ukraine's negotiating team maintained communication with Trump's team and even occasionally with Russian representatives, but the two sides remain far apart on key issues, according to Kakissis. Russia demands that Ukraine relinquish controlled land for a peace deal, but public opinion polls indicate that most Ukrainians strongly oppose this.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party has claimed a landslide victory &lt;/strong&gt;in the German state of Saxony-Anhalt, narrowly missing an absolute majority to form the regional government. It is unclear whether AfD will govern the state yet, but this outcome is shaking Germany's political landscape. If the AfD forms a governing coalition, it would establish the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/06/nx-s1-5955677/german-afd-far-right" target="_blank"&gt;first far-right regional government since Nazi Germany&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;NPR's Esme Nicholson says that politically&lt;/strong&gt;, these election results are "a disaster" for German Chanceller Freidrich Merz, who vowed to halve the number of AfD voters when he came into power. AfD can thank its candidate, 35-year-old Ulrich Siegmund, for &lt;a href="https://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5960265:x" target="_blank"&gt;pulling off this win&lt;/a&gt;, Nicholson says. He is a former marketing executive who shared feel-good videos on social media, vowing to "bring back the good old Germany." Despite his upbeat demeanor, he is not moderate, Nicholson says. Germany's domestic intelligence labels the AfD as "extremist" in Saxony-Anhalt. At the top of the party's agenda is "remigration," which promises mass deportations that will include those deemed to be unproductive, including Ukrainian refugees without jobs. The AfD also aims to segregate refugees and disabled children in schools and rework the curriculum to portray a more positive view of Germany's history.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Living better&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-141921" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3600;         --source-height: 2025;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2025+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F61%2F16%2F7e8fbf3f4cbcb25bb176e8db63fb%2Fhbarczyk-npr-dryeyes-finalart3.jpg" class="img" alt="hbarczyk_npr_dryeyes_finalart3.jpg" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Living Better is a &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/series/1176326550/living-better" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;special series&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; about what it takes to stay healthy in America.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Research suggests that about 50% of women going through the menopausal transition experience dry eye symptoms, including red, watery or gritty-feeling eyes. Hormonal changes play a significant role, but they aren't the only culprits — many other factors can contribute to this discomfort as well. Here's some of &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/04/nx-s1-5954560/dry-eyes-women-menopause-perimenopause" target="_blank"&gt;what you should know&lt;/a&gt; about the chronic condition:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;👁️ Dry eyes can affect work performance, reading, driving and other aspects of everyday life.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;👁️ A dry eye disease researcher warns that ignoring symptoms can worsen the condition and could eventually damage corneal surface cells.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;👁️ People can find relief through various treatments, such as warm compresses, over-the-counter eye drops and prescription medications. Reducing screen time can also help.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Picture show&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-140487" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4500;         --source-height: 2531;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2F53%2F3a12f9554231baf4c836fa2eddd2%2Frwanda-bridge-4077.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2F53%2F3a12f9554231baf4c836fa2eddd2%2Frwanda-bridge-4077.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2F53%2F3a12f9554231baf4c836fa2eddd2%2Frwanda-bridge-4077.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2F53%2F3a12f9554231baf4c836fa2eddd2%2Frwanda-bridge-4077.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2F53%2F3a12f9554231baf4c836fa2eddd2%2Frwanda-bridge-4077.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F66%2F53%2F3a12f9554231baf4c836fa2eddd2%2Frwanda-bridge-4077.jpg 1600w, 